---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Privacy Policy
description: What Net Cloud Edge collects when you send us a resume or a hiring brief, who we share it with, how long we keep it, and how to get it deleted.
effective: August 12, 2026
glass: true
extraScripts: []
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{#
  ⚠️ NOT LEGAL ADVICE. This is a drafted policy written against what the site actually
  does — the contact form, the resume upload, background checks run in connection with a
  placement — not a copied template. It must be reviewed by counsel before launch, and
  every bracketed or site.json placeholder confirmed (CONTENT.md verification list, item 14).

  Two rules held throughout: describe only processing that genuinely happens, and never
  promise a right the business cannot deliver. If a practice changes, this page changes
  with it — a policy that describes the wrong company is worse than no policy.

  No cover-sheet exhibit and no CTA band. A visitor who lands here wants a clause, not
  a photograph of an office and an invitation to book a call.

  Hallmark redesign — Centered Read. The old sticky 3/9 side-rail split is gone: the
  page is now one centered reading column (max-w-3xl, prose capped tighter at 40rem via
  .legal-prose). The rail's function moves to a "Contents" jump-link grid in a glass
  panel under the summary — same navigation, no permanent column, and it works on
  mobile where the rail was hidden entirely. Clauses are separated by a hairline rule
  rather than by whitespace alone. rail-active.js / section-rail.njk are no longer used
  here. `glass: true` still carries the ambient field for the summary, contents and
  contact panels; the header keeps the aurora/dots treatment.
#}

{% set rail = [
  { id: "scope",      label: "Who this covers",   n: "00" },
  { id: "collect",    label: "What we collect",   n: "A"  },
  { id: "use",        label: "How we use it",     n: "B"  },
  { id: "share",      label: "Who receives it",   n: "C"  },
  { id: "screening",  label: "Background checks", n: "D"  },
  { id: "cookies",    label: "Cookies",           n: "E"  },
  { id: "retention",  label: "How long we keep",  n: "F"  },
  { id: "security",   label: "Security",          n: "G"  },
  { id: "rights",     label: "Your rights",       n: "H"  },
  { id: "contact",    label: "Contact us",        n: "I"  }
] %}

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="hero-aurora" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="aurora-blob aurora-blob-1"></span>
    <span class="aurora-blob aurora-blob-2"></span>
    <span class="aurora-blob aurora-blob-3"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-dots" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="section-container py-10 sm:py-14">
    {% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Privacy Policy" }] %}
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <span class="stamp">{{ icon("check-badge", "w-3.5 h-3.5") }} On file</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/65">
          Effective {{ effective }} · {{ site.legalEntity }}
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
        We handle resumes for a living, so this page is specific: what we take, who we hand
        it to, how long we hold it, and how to make us delete it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-container pb-16 pt-4 sm:pb-24 sm:pt-8">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">

    {# The summary sits above the clauses, not in place of them. Most visitors read
       only this box; it has to be true on its own, not a gloss the clauses contradict. #}
    <div class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-7">
      <p class="meta">The short version</p>
      <div class="legal-prose mt-3">
        <p>
          We collect what you send us — contact details, a resume, a hiring brief — and use
          it to do the one job you asked for. We share a candidate's details with an employer
          only after that candidate agrees to that specific introduction. We run background
          checks only with written consent. We do not sell personal information, and we never
          charge a job seeker to be placed. You can ask us to delete your file at any time and
          we will, unless the law requires us to keep a record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Contents — replaces the old sticky side rail. A reader here is hunting one
       clause; a jump-link grid at the top does that without a permanent column. #}
    <nav class="mt-5 glass-panel p-6 sm:p-7" aria-label="Contents">
      <p class="meta">Contents</p>
      <ol class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-0.5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {% for item in rail %}
        <li>
          <a href="#{{ item.id }}" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 border-t border-ink/10 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink/75 transition-colors hover:text-brand">
            <span class="w-6 shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-ink/50">{{ item.n }}</span>
            {{ item.label }}
          </a>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    {# ---- 00 Scope ---- #}
      <div id="scope" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">00 — Scope</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Who this covers.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            This policy explains how {{ site.legalEntity }} (&ldquo;{{ site.shortName }},&rdquo;
            &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;) handles personal information. It applies to
            <a href="{{ site.url }}">{{ site.url }}</a>, to our recruitment, staffing, talent
            acquisition, background verification and IT training services, and to email, phone
            and in-person contact with us about any of them.
          </p>
          <p>It covers four groups of people:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Candidates</strong> — anyone who sends us a resume, applies through us, or is put forward to an employer by us.</li>
            <li><strong>Client contacts</strong> — the people at employers who brief us, interview our candidates, and sign our agreements.</li>
            <li><strong>Training applicants and learners</strong> — anyone who enquires about or enrols in one of our programs.</li>
            <li><strong>Site visitors</strong> — anyone who reads these pages without contacting us.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Where we recruit for an employer, that employer decides what it does with the
            candidate information we pass on. From that point the employer is responsible for
            its own handling of it, under its own privacy policy — not this one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- A What we collect. A table, because the honest answer differs by who you
             are, and a paragraph that tries to cover all four groups at once ends up
             covering none of them. ---- #}
      <div id="collect" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">A — Collection</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          What we collect.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            Almost all of it comes directly from you. We do not buy candidate lists.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="ledger">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Category</th>
                <th scope="col">What that means</th>
                <th scope="col">Where it comes from</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Contact details</th>
                <td>Name, email address, phone number, city.</td>
                <td>You, via the contact form, email or a call.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Career history</th>
                <td>Your resume and anything in it — employment history, education, certifications, skills, references.</td>
                <td>You, or a referrer you asked to send it.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Placement record</th>
                <td>Roles you were put forward for, interview outcomes, notes from our conversations, availability, and the terms you told us you would accept.</td>
                <td>Generated by us as we work your file.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Verification data</th>
                <td>Identity, employment and education checks, and — where a role requires it and you have consented in writing — criminal record and credit checks.</td>
                <td>Screening vendors, former employers, institutions.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Client details</th>
                <td>Company name, the role being hired for, business contact details, and the commercial terms of our engagement.</td>
                <td>The employer.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Training records</th>
                <td>Track enrolled in, attendance, assessment results, and payment status.</td>
                <td>You, and our instructors.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" data-rowhead>Technical data</th>
                <td>IP address, browser and device type, pages viewed, and the site you arrived from.</td>
                <td>Collected automatically — see <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <h3>Sensitive information</h3>
          <p>
            Some of what a resume contains is sensitive — date of birth, national identifiers,
            work authorisation status, and in some jurisdictions criminal history. We ask for
            these only where a role or the law genuinely requires them, we ask separately rather
            than burying the request in a form, and we do not use them for anything but the
            purpose we asked for. Please do not send us health information, and do not include
            it on a resume you upload here.
          </p>
          <h3>Children</h3>
          <p>
            Our services are for working-age adults. We do not knowingly collect information
            from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has sent us information, write to
            <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we will delete it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- B How we use it ---- #}
      <div id="use" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">B — Purpose</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          How we use it.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>We use personal information to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reply to your enquiry and work out whether we can help.</li>
            <li>Match candidates to open roles and put a shortlist to an employer.</li>
            <li>Prepare a candidate for interview and pass on feedback afterwards.</li>
            <li>Run background verification where a role requires it and consent has been given.</li>
            <li>Deliver, assess and administer training programs, including payment.</li>
            <li>Keep a record of who we introduced to whom, which is how placement fees are established and disputed.</li>
            <li>Meet legal obligations — tax, employment, anti-discrimination and record-keeping law.</li>
            <li>Understand which parts of this site are used, in aggregate, so we can improve it.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>What we do not do</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.</li>
            <li>We do not send a resume to an employer without the candidate's agreement to that specific introduction.</li>
            <li>We do not make hiring decisions by automated means. Software helps us search and sort; a person decides who is put forward.</li>
            <li>We do not charge job seekers. Our fee is paid by the employer.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Marketing</h3>
          <p>
            We may email you about roles, programs or hiring updates relevant to what you came
            to us for. Every such email carries an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing does not
            affect the service you are already receiving from us.
          </p>
          <h3>Legal bases</h3>
          <p>
            Where the UK or EU GDPR applies to you, we rely on: <strong>contract</strong>, to
            provide a service you asked for; <strong>legitimate interests</strong>, to operate a
            recruitment business, keep our records, and secure this site; <strong>consent</strong>,
            for background checks, marketing email and non-essential cookies, which you may
            withdraw at any time; and <strong>legal obligation</strong>, where a law requires us
            to collect or keep something.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- C Sharing ---- #}
      <div id="share" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">C — Disclosure</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Who receives it.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Employers and their hiring teams</strong>, when a candidate has agreed to be put forward for that specific role. We tell you which employer before we send anything.</li>
            <li><strong>Screening vendors</strong>, to run the checks described below.</li>
            <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who run parts of our operation under contract — email, applicant tracking, cloud hosting, accounting, payment processing. They may use the information only to perform that service for us.</li>
            <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> — lawyers, auditors, insurers — where we need advice or have to prove something.</li>
            <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, where the law compels disclosure or we need to establish, exercise or defend a legal claim.</li>
            <li><strong>A buyer</strong>, if the business or part of it is sold or merged. The information stays subject to this policy until you are told otherwise.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>International transfers</h3>
          <p>
            We are based in {{ site.address.line2 }}, and some of our providers operate outside
            your country. Where we move personal information across a border we use a lawful
            transfer mechanism — standard contractual clauses or an adequacy decision — and
            require the recipient to protect it to the standard set out here.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- D Background verification. This is a service we sell, so it gets its own
             clause rather than a line in the sharing list. The FCRA language is
             US-specific and is exactly what counsel must check first. ---- #}
      <div id="screening" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">D — Verification</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Background checks.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            Background verification is checking we run in connection with a placement, and it is
            the most intrusive thing we do with your information. It runs on rules:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Nothing is checked without your <strong>written consent</strong>, given separately from any job application, and describing what will be checked.</li>
            <li>You are told which vendor will perform the check before it begins.</li>
            <li>You may withdraw consent at any point before the check completes. We will stop; the employer may then decide it cannot proceed with the role.</li>
            <li>You get a copy of the report on request, and a reasonable opportunity to dispute anything in it before it counts against you.</li>
            <li>Where a check is a &ldquo;consumer report&rdquo; under the US Fair Credit Reporting Act, you also receive the disclosures and the summary of rights that Act requires, and the adverse-action process it sets out is followed before a decision is finalised.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We check only what the role justifies. A credit check on a role with no financial
            responsibility is not something we will run, whoever asks for it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- E Cookies. Written against what the site actually loads today: no
             analytics, no ad pixels, one CDN font request. If a tag is ever added,
             this clause and the retention table change in the same commit. ---- #}
      <div id="cookies" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">E — Cookies</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Cookies and tracking.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            This site is deliberately light. We set no advertising cookies and we do not track
            you across other websites. What runs is:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Strictly necessary</strong> storage, to keep the site working and secure. It cannot be switched off, and it identifies nobody.</li>
            <li><strong>Aggregate analytics</strong>, if enabled, to count page views and referrers. We configure it to anonymise IP addresses and we do not use it to build a profile of you.</li>
            <li><strong>Fonts</strong>, requested from Google Fonts. Loading a font tells Google your IP address; nothing else is sent, and no cookie is set by it.</li>
            <li><strong>Server logs</strong>, kept by our host for security and troubleshooting.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Your browser can block or delete cookies, and most honour a Global Privacy Control
            signal, which we treat as a valid opt-out of any sale or sharing — though as above,
            we do neither.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- F Retention ---- #}
      <div id="retention" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">F — Retention</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          How long we keep it.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            We keep a file for as long as it is useful to the purpose it was collected for, then
            we delete it. In practice:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="ledger">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Record</th>
                <th scope="col">Kept for</th>
                <th scope="col">Why</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Enquiry with no engagement</th>
                <td>12 months</td>
                <td>So we recognise you if you come back.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Active candidate file</th>
                <td>24 months from last contact</td>
                <td>To put you forward for later roles.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Placement record</th>
                <td>7 years from placement</td>
                <td>Fee entitlement, tax and employment law.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Verification report</th>
                <td>As required by the check's governing law</td>
                <td>Statutory minimum, then destroyed.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Training and payment records</th>
                <td>7 years</td>
                <td>Accounting and certification.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Server logs</th>
                <td>90 days</td>
                <td>Security and troubleshooting.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            Ask us to delete your file earlier and we will, except for the minimum we are
            legally required to retain — typically a placement record. We will tell you what is
            being kept and why.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- G Security ---- #}
      <div id="security" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">G — Security</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          How we protect it.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            Access to candidate files is limited to the people working your case. Data is
            encrypted in transit, our providers are contracted to security terms, and accounts
            carry multi-factor authentication. Staff are trained on handling resumes and
            verification reports specifically.
          </p>
          <p>
            No system is perfectly secure, and we will not claim otherwise. If a breach affects
            your information and puts you at risk, we will notify you and the relevant regulator
            within the timeframe the law sets.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- H Rights. Deliberately written as one list rather than split by
             jurisdiction: a candidate should not have to work out which statute
             applies to them before they can ask for their file back. ---- #}
      <div id="rights" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">H — Rights</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Your rights.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, you have some or all of the rights below. We extend all
            of them to every candidate as a matter of practice, rather than asking you to prove
            which law covers you.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Know and access</strong> — what we hold about you, and a copy of it.</li>
            <li><strong>Correct</strong> — fix anything inaccurate, which matters most for a resume already in circulation.</li>
            <li><strong>Delete</strong> — have your file erased, subject to the retention table above.</li>
            <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — for background checks or marketing, at any time.</li>
            <li><strong>Object or restrict</strong> — tell us to stop a particular use while a question is resolved.</li>
            <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive what you gave us in a machine-readable file.</li>
            <li><strong>Opt out of sale or sharing</strong> — already the default; we do neither.</li>
            <li><strong>Non-retaliation</strong> — exercising any of these will not affect how we represent you.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To use any of them, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> with
            enough detail for us to find your file. We respond within 45 days, and will tell you
            if we need longer. We may ask you to verify your identity first — we are not handing
            a resume to whoever asks for it. An authorised agent may act for you with written
            permission.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are unhappy with our answer, you may complain to your data protection
            authority: in the EU or UK, your national regulator; in California, the California
            Privacy Protection Agency or the Attorney General.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# ---- I Contact and changes ---- #}
      <div id="contact" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">I — Contact</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-xl font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
          Changes, and how to reach us.
        </h2>
        <div class="legal-prose mt-6">
          <p>
            We update this policy when our practices change. The effective date at the top of the
            page always reflects the current version, and if a change materially affects how we
            handle candidate information we will say so directly to the people concerned rather
            than relying on you to re-read this page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 glass-panel p-6">
          <p class="meta">Privacy enquiries</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon("mail", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
              <div>
                <dt class="meta">Email</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-sm"><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="text-ink/75 transition-colors hover:text-brand">{{ site.email }}</a></dd>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon("map-pin", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
              <div>
                <dt class="meta">Post</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/75">{{ site.legalEntity }}<br>{{ site.address.line1 }}<br>{{ site.address.line2 }}</dd>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon("phone", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
              <div>
                <dt class="meta">Phone</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-sm"><a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}" class="text-ink/75 transition-colors hover:text-brand">{{ site.phone }}</a></dd>
              </div>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-6 border-t border-dashed border-border pt-5 body-copy">
            Read this alongside our <a href="{{ '/terms-conditions/' | url }}" class="font-medium text-brand hover:underline">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

  </div>
</section>
